ed on the north side of Antioch.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"IL","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"LOT"},{"begin":"2026-04-03T01:05Z","county":"Kenosha","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"70.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-03T01:11Z","endLat":42.6094,"endLon":-87.8272,"episode":212464,"id":1329050,"injuries":0,"lat":42.5897,"location":"2.08 WNW Downtown Kenosha","lon":-87.8686,"magnitude":78.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"A swath of straight-line wind damage was observed. Dozens of trees were uprooted and widespread large limb damage occurred. A partial loss of roof shingles and fascia on several homes, and a partial loss of siding on some homes. A few small sheds were destroyed and several power lines were downed. 2200 We Energies customers were without power. The greatest concentration of damage was near the intersection of 45th Street and 38th Avenue.","source":"NWS Storm Survey","state":"WI","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"MKX"},{"begin":"2026-04-03T01:05Z","county":"Tangipahoa","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-03T02:05Z","endLat":30.6422,"endLon":-90.5195,"episode":213194,"id":1334827,"injuries":0,"lat":30.64,"location":"0.91 NW Independence","lon":-90.51,"narrative":"Public reported roads in Independence covered with water with vehicles taking on water along Hwy 40. Reported via social media.","source":"Public","state":"LA","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"LIX"},{"begin":"2026-04-03T01:11Z","county":"Du Page","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-03T01:11Z","endLat":41.8686,"endLon":-88.0309,"episode":211371,"id":1331385,"injuries":0,"lat":41.8686,"location":"0.11 SSW Flowerfield","lon":-88.0309,"magnitude":56.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Multiple reports were received of trees and tree branches down at and near Sunset Knoll Park in Lombard.","source":"Public","state":"IL","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"LOT"},{"begin":"2026-04-03T01:11Z","county":"Du Page","dama